OCPP Hub builds on ideas and the snoop stream format of ha-ocpp-relay
(https://github.com/michael-adler/ha-ocpp-relay), which is released under the MIT
license reproduced below. Code adapted from that project keeps this notice.

The way the hub treats a charger after it connects (asking a charger that sends no boot or status for them
with TriggerMessage, waiting before the first request, notifying the owner when a charger connects) follows
what lbbrhzn/ocpp (https://github.com/lbbrhzn/ocpp, MIT, Copyright (c) 2021 lbbrhzn) does on real chargers.
That is behaviour learned from it; no code has been copied. Code adapted from it would keep its MIT notice.

